1
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:08,060
In the old times,  whenever Braavos stood in danger,

2
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:12,930
the Titan would step with fire in his eyes.

3
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:16,020
He'd wade into the sea and smash the enemies.

4
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:18,920
He's a statue.

5
00:02:24,070 --> 00:02:27,680
Don't be afraid. He's announcing our arrival.

6
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,220
I'm not afraid.

7
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:41,750
The House of Black and White.

8
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,400
This is where you'll find the man you seek.

9
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:52,770
Here I leave you.

10
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:02,060
Thank you for bringing me.

11
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,660
Any man of Braavos would have done the same.

12
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:10,120
- Valar morghulis. - Valar dohaeris.

13
00:04:45,970 --> 00:04:46,920
Hello.

14
00:04:50,830 --> 00:04:52,380
Valar morghulis.

15
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,140
Jaqen H'ghar gave me this.

16
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:12,820
- No one here by that name. - Please!

17
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,910
I've crossed the narrow sea. I have nowhere else to go.

18
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:20,320
- You have everywhere else to go. - But wait!

19
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:41,990
Cersei...

20
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,310
Walder Frey...

21
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:47,040
The Mountain...

22
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,050
Meryn Trant.

23
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,950
Cersei...

24
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:56,170
Walder Frey...

25
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,970
The Mountain...

26
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,320
Meryn Trant.

27
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:03,600
Cersei...

28
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,070
Walder Frey...

29
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:06,550
The Mountain...

30
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,070
Meryn Trant.

31
00:06:11,110 --> 00:06:12,120
Cersei...

32
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:13,950
Walder Frey...

33
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:15,630
The Mountain...

34
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,430
Meryn Trant.

35
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,630
Cersei...

36
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,280
Walder Frey...

37
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:25,230
The Mountain...

38
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,470
Meryn Trant...

39
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:01,840
Must be good food if it's crowded.

40
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:08,040
Ale?

41
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:16,800
Ale?

42
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,370
Before we left, a maester gave you a raven's scroll.

43
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:33,460
You are becoming an observant young lady.

44
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:36,160
My mother used to say "dark wings, dark words".

45
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:39,770
An old saying. Inaccurate in this case.

46
00:07:42,850 --> 00:07:44,230
So it's good news.

47
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:47,000
My marriage proposal has been accepted.

48
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:49,930
I thought you still mourned the death of my beloved Aunt Lysa.

49
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:52,680
- Ale? - I'll have some.

50
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:57,950
My Lady...

51
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:02,220
- What is it? - Sansa Stark. Don't look!

52
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:04,670
You sure?

53
00:08:04,670 --> 00:08:06,190
She's dyed her hair, but it's her.

54
00:08:06,190 --> 00:08:07,880
She's sitting with Petyr Baelish.

55
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:09,020
Littlefinger?

56
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:10,700
A bunch of knights with them.

57
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:12,740
A bunch? What's a bunch, Podrick? Six? Twenty?

58
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:14,630
Ten, I think. Too many.

59
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:16,130
My Lady, I don't think this is the right...

60
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:17,750
Ready the horses!

61
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,350
We only have one horse.

62
00:08:19,350 --> 00:08:20,970
Find more!

63
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:28,350
Do you like the taste?

64
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:30,860
Don't see what all the fuss is about.

65
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,110
Why do men love it so much?

66
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:36,270
It gives some men courage.

67
00:08:36,270 --> 00:08:37,980
Does it give you courage?

68
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,260
That's far enough.

69
00:08:44,050 --> 00:08:45,350
Lord Baelish.

70
00:08:45,850 --> 00:08:47,000
Lady Sansa.

71
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:49,410
My name is Brienne of Tarth.

72
00:08:49,410 --> 00:08:51,930
We've met with Renly Baratheon.

73
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,360
What did he say about you?

74
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:55,910
He said,

75
00:08:57,130 --> 00:09:00,010
your loyalty came free of charge.

76
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:03,980
Someone appears to have paid quite a bit for it since then.

77
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:18,840
Lady Sansa,

78
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:22,190
before your mother's death,

79
00:09:22,190 --> 00:09:24,040
I was her sworn sword.

80
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:28,040
I gave my word I will find you and protect you.

81
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,900
I will shield your back and keep your counsel,

82
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:33,280
and give my life for yours if need be.

83
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:37,010
I swear it by the Old Gods and the New.

84
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:40,070
Please, lady Brienne.

85
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:41,750
No need for such formality.

86
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:44,560
You were Catelyn Stark's sworn sword.

87
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,760
- I was. - Strange.

88
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:48,070
I knew Cat from the time we were children.

89
00:09:48,070 --> 00:09:49,350
She never mentioned you.

90
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:52,020
It was after Renly's murder.

91
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:53,480
Ah, yes.

92
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,270
You were accused of killing him.

93
00:09:55,270 --> 00:09:56,690
I tried to save him.

94
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:59,990
- But you were accused. - By men who did not see what happened.

95
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,500
And what did happen?

96
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:07,990
He was murdered by a shadow.

97
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:11,620
A shadow with the face of Stannis Baratheon.

98
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:12,850
A shadow?

99
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,240
With the face...

100
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:21,480
This woman swore to protect Renly,

101
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,670
she failed.

102
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:24,540
She swore to protect your mother,

103
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,490
she failed.

104
00:10:26,490 --> 00:10:30,010
Why would I want somebody with your history of failure guarding Lady Sansa?

105
00:10:30,010 --> 00:10:32,080
Why should you have any say in her affairs?

106
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,850
Because I am her uncle.

107
00:10:33,850 --> 00:10:37,620
I married her Aunt Lysa shortly before my beloved's untimely death.

108
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:40,400
We're family now  and you are an outsider.

109
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,550
Forgive me, Lady Brienne.

110
00:10:41,550 --> 00:10:44,750
But experience has made me wary of outsiders.

111
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:46,210
Lady Sansa...

112
00:10:46,210 --> 00:10:48,340
- if we can have a word alone... - No.

113
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:50,090
Please, my Lady, if I I could explain...

114
00:10:50,090 --> 00:10:51,990
I saw you at Joffrey's wedding...

115
00:10:51,990 --> 00:10:53,480
bowing to the king.

116
00:10:53,490 --> 00:10:55,400
Neither of us wanted to be there.

117
00:10:56,950 --> 00:11:00,040
- Sometimes we don't have a choice. - And sometimes we do.

118
00:11:01,910 --> 00:11:03,280
You should leave.

119
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:07,400
We don't want our new friend wandering the countryside alone.

120
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,850
The roads in these parts aren't safe.

121
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:11,070
Why don't you stay?

122
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,360
The man asked you to stay--

123
00:12:09,910 --> 00:12:12,100
- Stop! Stop! - After him!

124
00:12:13,530 --> 00:12:14,610
Podrick!

125
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,210
Hold on to her.

126
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:55,270
Stop, stop, stop, stop! Stop!

127
00:12:58,730 --> 00:13:00,490
That's a good boy. Come on.

128
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:01,440
Come on!

129
00:13:03,870 --> 00:13:05,270
No, no, no, stop!

130
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:27,370
Guess that means you're unarmed.

131
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:30,100
Down! Podrick down!

132
00:13:49,850 --> 00:13:50,840
Podrick?

133
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:52,770
Yes, my Lady?

134
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:54,620
You can stand now.

135
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,480
Yes, my Lady.

136
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:01,850
Sansa Stark?

137
00:14:03,110 --> 00:14:05,220
Wary of strangers, as she should be.

138
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:08,240
I saw her riding on the east road with Littlefinger.

139
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,250
- We'll follow them. - My Lady...

140
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:13,140
if both Stark girls refused your service,

141
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,760
maybe you're released from your vow.

142
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:17,600
I swore to their mother I would protect those girls.

143
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,860
But if they don't want your protection.

144
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:20,760
Do you think she's safe with Littlefinger?

145
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:24,750
No, my Lady.

146
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,440
Get your horse.

147
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,830
A summons from the Queen.

148
00:14:56,550 --> 00:14:58,800
There are only two like it in the world.

149
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:02,100
The one I'm wearing,  the one I gave to Myrcella.

150
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:03,710
It's a threat.

151
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:05,310
Of course it's a threat.

152
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:07,580
Our daughter is alone in Dorne

153
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:10,360
surrounded by people who hate our family.

154
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:12,520
It's a threat.

155
00:15:15,130 --> 00:15:15,960
No note?

156
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:19,280
They blame us for the death of Oberyn and his sister,

157
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:22,330
and every other tragedy that's befallen their cursed country.

158
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:25,100
I will burn their cities to the ground if they touch her.

159
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,950
- Softer. - What?

160
00:15:26,950 --> 00:15:27,890
Not so loud.

161
00:15:27,890 --> 00:15:28,870
Our daughter is in danger

162
00:15:28,870 --> 00:15:30,800
and you're worried I am speaking too loudly?

163
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:33,400
The world can't know she's our daughter.

164
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,980
Then don't call her your daughter.

165
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:38,240
You've never been a father to her.

166
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:40,080
If I was a father to any of my children,

167
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,290
they'd be stoned in the street.

168
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:42,940
And what has your caution brought?

169
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:47,330
Our eldest child murdered at his own wedding,

170
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,170
our only daughter shipped off to Dorne,

171
00:15:51,430 --> 00:15:55,550
our baby boy set to marry that smirking whore from Highgarden!

172
00:16:04,830 --> 00:16:06,100
I'm going to make things better.

173
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,470
You've never made anything better.

174
00:16:07,470 --> 00:16:08,610
I'm going to Dorne.

175
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:10,830
And I'm bringing our daughter home.

176
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,500
You can't just ask Prince Doran to give her back.

177
00:16:15,990 --> 00:16:17,850
She's promised to his son.

178
00:16:17,850 --> 00:16:19,860
I'm not going to ask him anything.

179
00:16:20,470 --> 00:16:22,530
You go down there with an army, it's an act of war.

180
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:23,510
No army.

181
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:25,910
Do you know where they're keeping her?

182
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:31,780
Oberyn mentioned the Water Gardens.

183
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:32,820
I'll find her.

184
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,550
Is there anything else, Your Grace?

185
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:42,470
You're going to Dorne.

186
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,420
A one-handed man,

187
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,360
alone?

188
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:50,210
Never said I was going alone.

189
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,260
No sunfloweres. I don't like yellow.

190
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,540
Roses are very nice, definitely roses.

191
00:17:03,550 --> 00:17:05,190
And music. I adore music.

192
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,510
But no flutes.

193
00:17:06,510 --> 00:17:07,490
I hate flutes.

194
00:17:07,490 --> 00:17:09,480
We can have a harp, if you like, but no flutes.

195
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:10,410
Then there's the food.

196
00:17:10,410 --> 00:17:12,610
The food is the most important thing, don't you agree?

197
00:17:12,610 --> 00:17:14,520
We're going to need pigeon pies.

198
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:17,070
That's what they eat in the capital, don't they?

199
00:17:18,310 --> 00:17:19,320
Don't they?

200
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:22,320
Don't who?

201
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:25,320
People eat pigeon pie in the capital.

202
00:17:26,470 --> 00:17:28,290
They certainly do, my dear.

203
00:17:28,290 --> 00:17:29,470
They certainly do.

204
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:32,590
It's a fine place, isn't it?

205
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:34,860
A fine place.

206
00:17:35,350 --> 00:17:38,970
I never thought I'd end up settling down in a place like this.

207
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:40,860
You won't.

208
00:17:42,310 --> 00:17:43,150
Pardon?

209
00:17:43,150 --> 00:17:45,060
We won't get to live at Stokeworth.

210
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:48,570
When mother dies, my sister gets the castle because she's older.

211
00:17:48,570 --> 00:17:50,050
She hates me.

212
00:17:50,050 --> 00:17:51,760
She calls me mean names and sometimes

213
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:54,730
even still she pulls my hair when mother's not looking.

214
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:57,990
You know what I think?

215
00:17:58,850 --> 00:18:01,040
I think you're a good person.

216
00:18:01,050 --> 00:18:03,350
And your sister is a mean person.

217
00:18:03,350 --> 00:18:04,340
She is.

218
00:18:06,910 --> 00:18:08,520
I've been all over the world,

219
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:10,660
and if there's one thing I've learned,

220
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:12,660
it's that meanness comes around.

221
00:18:13,890 --> 00:18:15,260
People like your sister,

222
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:18,420
they always get what's coming to them eventually.

223
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:20,890
One way or another.

224
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:25,810
Who's that?

225
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:30,840
Jaime fucking Lannister.

226
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:33,980
Ser Jaime?

227
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,440
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater.

228
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:39,640
I was very sorry to hear about your father.

229
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,570
Thank you.

230
00:18:41,390 --> 00:18:43,960
This is my betrothed Lollys.

231
00:18:45,690 --> 00:18:46,720
A pleasure.

232
00:18:49,730 --> 00:18:50,940
Run along, love.

233
00:18:57,670 --> 00:18:59,680
Beautiful young bride you've chosen.

234
00:19:00,410 --> 00:19:02,020
When were you planning on getting married?

235
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:03,310
Just get on with it.

236
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:04,460
On with what?

237
00:19:04,460 --> 00:19:05,780
What you're here for.

238
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:07,220
There's no way this little visit

239
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,230
could possibly mean anything good for me.

240
00:19:09,230 --> 00:19:10,680
It's very good for you.

241
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:25,970
Lollys will be marrying Ser Willis Bracken.

242
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:29,280
We've made a deal, your sister and I.

243
00:19:30,110 --> 00:19:31,760
I would have advised against that.

244
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:32,810
How is this good for me?

245
00:19:32,810 --> 00:19:33,790
Because you're going to come with me

246
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,780
and help me with something important.

247
00:19:36,010 --> 00:19:37,380
And when we return,

248
00:19:37,390 --> 00:19:41,350
I'm going to give you a much better girl and a much better castle.

249
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:45,610
Return from where?

250
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:48,710
As far south as south goes.

251
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:15,040
You are my queen.

252
00:20:23,830 --> 00:20:26,230
The prince does not wish to be disturbed.

253
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:27,730
Remove yourself from my path

254
00:20:27,730 --> 00:20:29,830
or I'll take that long axe and I'll shove it up your...

255
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:30,920
Captain.

256
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,230
let her pass.

257
00:20:38,550 --> 00:20:40,230
Your brother was murdered

258
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:43,170
and you sit here in the Water Gardens

259
00:20:43,170 --> 00:20:45,420
staring at the sky and doing nothing.

260
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:48,440
Oberyn was slain during a trial by combat.

261
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,620
By law, that is no murder.

262
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:52,250
- Your brother... - You don't have to remind me.

263
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:55,540
He was my brother long before he was anything to you.

264
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:57,070
What will you do about his death?

265
00:20:57,070 --> 00:20:59,910
I will bury him. I will mourn for him.

266
00:20:59,910 --> 00:21:00,890
And then?

267
00:21:00,890 --> 00:21:02,260
You would have me go to war.

268
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:03,810
The whole country would have you go to war.

269
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:07,020
Then we are lucky the whole country does not decide.

270
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,870
The Sand Snakes are with me.

271
00:21:11,010 --> 00:21:12,670
They have the love of their people.

272
00:21:12,710 --> 00:21:13,940
They will avenge their father

273
00:21:13,950 --> 00:21:18,120
while you sit here in your chair doing nothing.

274
00:21:22,390 --> 00:21:23,880
Oberyn is dead.

275
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:27,840
And this Lannister girl skips about the Water Gardens

276
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:31,090
eating our food, breathing our air.

277
00:21:32,050 --> 00:21:33,690
How many of your brothers and sisters

278
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:35,140
do they have to kill?

279
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:37,610
Let me have her.

280
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:43,840
Let me send her to Cersei one finger at a time.

281
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,630
I loved my brother.

282
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:49,650
And you made him very happy.

283
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:52,440
For that, you will always have a place in my heart.

284
00:21:53,670 --> 00:21:57,700
But we do not mutilate little girls for vengeance.

285
00:21:58,070 --> 00:21:59,200
Not here.

286
00:21:59,830 --> 00:22:01,340
Not while I rule.

287
00:22:02,770 --> 00:22:04,510
And how long will that be?

288
00:22:20,930 --> 00:22:23,040
The Unsullied are too conspicuous.

289
00:22:23,460 --> 00:22:25,770
Anyone can see them coming from a mile off.

290
00:22:26,280 --> 00:22:28,560
'Course you haven't found any Sons of the Harpy.

291
00:22:28,990 --> 00:22:30,280
You haven't, have you?

292
00:22:32,610 --> 00:22:34,880
My Second Sons, on the other hand,

293
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:39,810
they drink, they whore, fight in the streets,

294
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:41,710
they blend in.

295
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:43,870
They overhear things in taverns.

296
00:22:44,190 --> 00:22:47,580
Follow people from the taverns to nice, quiet alleys.

297
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:52,080
Break a few fingers, overhear a few more things.

298
00:22:53,350 --> 00:22:54,670
Before you know it...

299
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:15,880
No one here.

300
00:23:16,850 --> 00:23:18,030
We go.

301
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,470
In a hurry?

302
00:23:19,890 --> 00:23:20,870
You're afraid?

303
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:23,070
Unsullied fear nothing.

304
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,290
Right.

305
00:23:25,730 --> 00:23:27,080
That's your problem.

306
00:23:27,310 --> 00:23:29,710
You understood fear once, long ago,

307
00:23:29,710 --> 00:23:31,250
but you've forgotten what it means.

308
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:34,110
Someone who has forgotten fear

309
00:23:34,870 --> 00:23:36,510
has forgotten how to hide.

310
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:47,410
Fear is useful that way.

311
00:24:12,130 --> 00:24:13,540
Sons of the Harpy...

312
00:24:13,540 --> 00:24:15,740
they want to put a collar back on my neck.

313
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,180
On all of our necks. Please, Your Grace...

314
00:24:18,180 --> 00:24:20,580
- you must kill him. - It would send a message.

315
00:24:20,650 --> 00:24:22,820
I think you should exercise restraint...

316
00:24:22,820 --> 00:24:23,910
- Your Grace. - Why?

317
00:24:23,910 --> 00:24:26,090
Well, for one thing, he may have valuable information.

318
00:24:26,090 --> 00:24:29,230
Well, the Son of the Harpy has no more valuable information.

319
00:24:29,230 --> 00:24:30,370
How do you know that?

320
00:24:30,370 --> 00:24:32,120
Because I questioned him.

321
00:24:32,830 --> 00:24:35,250
And the information you did get... he is young and poor

322
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:36,280
He is born free.

323
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:37,520
Why should he want to bring back slavery?

324
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:38,570
What did it do for him?

325
00:24:38,570 --> 00:24:40,030
Perhaps the only thing that gave him pride

326
00:24:40,030 --> 00:24:41,940
was knowing that there was someone lower than he was.

327
00:24:41,940 --> 00:24:43,250
They pay him.

328
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:45,560
Great families, afraid to do a thing.

329
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:46,860
They pay poor men to do it for them.

330
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:47,950
And how do you know this?

331
00:24:47,950 --> 00:24:49,740
- Everyone know this. - I don't know it.

332
00:24:49,740 --> 00:24:51,000
And I'm the head of a great family.

333
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:53,490
We do not know what this man did or didn't do.

334
00:24:53,490 --> 00:24:55,620
Give him a trial at least.

335
00:24:55,630 --> 00:24:57,000
A fair trial.

336
00:24:57,810 --> 00:24:59,350
Show all the citizens of Meereen

337
00:24:59,350 --> 00:25:01,810
that you are better than those who would depose you.

338
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:03,150
Teach them a better way.

339
00:25:03,150 --> 00:25:05,780
I do not know the place from where old ser comes.

340
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:08,510
Things maybe are different there, I hope.

341
00:25:09,080 --> 00:25:11,020
But here in Meereen,

342
00:25:11,020 --> 00:25:12,400
before Daenerys Stormborn

343
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,700
they own us.

344
00:25:14,140 --> 00:25:16,190
So we learn much about them...

345
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:18,020
or we do not live long.

346
00:25:18,630 --> 00:25:20,650
They teach me what they are.

347
00:25:21,110 --> 00:25:23,390
Mercy, fair trial...

348
00:25:23,390 --> 00:25:25,210
these mean nothing to them.

349
00:25:25,210 --> 00:25:27,350
All they understand is blood.

350
00:25:32,690 --> 00:25:34,260
Thank you all for your counsel.

351
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:44,350
Your Grace...

352
00:25:44,350 --> 00:25:45,860
a word, please, I beg you.

353
00:25:45,860 --> 00:25:46,880
About what?

354
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:48,260
About your father.

355
00:25:48,530 --> 00:25:50,560
- About the Mad King. - The Mad King?

356
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:52,400
You're here to remind me of my enemies' lies?

357
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,530
Consider me reminded.

358
00:25:53,530 --> 00:25:54,670
Your Grace...

359
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:57,280
I served in his Kingsguard.

360
00:25:58,030 --> 00:26:00,040
I was at his side from the first.

361
00:26:00,040 --> 00:26:01,640
Your enemies did not lie.

362
00:26:03,910 --> 00:26:05,020
Go on.

363
00:26:07,110 --> 00:26:09,630
When the people rose in revolt against him,

364
00:26:09,970 --> 00:26:12,480
your father set their towns and castles aflame.

365
00:26:13,520 --> 00:26:16,040
He murdered sons in front of their fathers.

366
00:26:16,940 --> 00:26:19,280
He burned men alive with wildfire

367
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:21,070
and laughed as they screamed,

368
00:26:22,210 --> 00:26:24,590
and his efforts to stamp out dissent

369
00:26:25,670 --> 00:26:28,430
led to a rebellion that killed every Targaryen...

370
00:26:28,840 --> 00:26:30,140
except two.

371
00:26:31,300 --> 00:26:32,640
I'm not my father.

372
00:26:32,870 --> 00:26:35,420
No, Your Grace, thank the gods.

373
00:26:36,420 --> 00:26:40,350
But the Mad King gave his enemies the justice he thought they deserved.

374
00:26:40,530 --> 00:26:43,240
And each time, it made him feel powerful

375
00:26:43,380 --> 00:26:44,600
and right.

376
00:26:45,660 --> 00:26:47,110
until the very end.

377
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:54,130
I will not have the Son of the Harpy executed

378
00:26:54,130 --> 00:26:55,530
without a fair trial.

379
00:26:59,600 --> 00:27:00,710
Your Grace.

380
00:27:10,820 --> 00:27:11,990
There's a bug.

381
00:27:12,100 --> 00:27:13,640
Yes, best be careful.

382
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:16,450
You might accidentally consume some solid food.

383
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:18,430
When I agreed to come with you,

384
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:21,260
did I misrepresent my intentions?

385
00:27:25,510 --> 00:27:26,530
Besides,

386
00:27:27,210 --> 00:27:30,640
what else is there for me to do inside this fucking box?

387
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:32,780
- You don't like it? - I want to take a walk.

388
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:33,830
You can't.

389
00:27:33,830 --> 00:27:37,130
Cersei has offered a lordship to the man who brings her your head.

390
00:27:37,130 --> 00:27:39,070
She ought to offer her cunt.

391
00:27:39,540 --> 00:27:41,920
Best part of her for the best part of me.

392
00:27:42,580 --> 00:27:45,940
Well, I suppose a box is as good a place for me as anywhere.

393
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:49,270
Are we really going to spend the entire road to Volantis

394
00:27:49,270 --> 00:27:51,400
talking about the futility of everything.

395
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:53,160
You're right, there's no point.

396
00:27:53,670 --> 00:27:55,580
The road to Volantis?

397
00:27:55,670 --> 00:27:58,590
You said we were going to Meereen. What's in Volantis?

398
00:27:58,590 --> 00:28:00,140
The road to Meereen.

399
00:28:00,140 --> 00:28:03,830
And what do you hope to find at the end on the road to Meereen?

400
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:05,920
I told you. A ruler.

401
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:07,800
We've already got a ruler.

402
00:28:08,120 --> 00:28:10,540
Everywhere has already got a ruler.

403
00:28:10,840 --> 00:28:13,560
Every pile of shit on the side of every road

404
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:15,530
has someone's banner hanging from it.

405
00:28:15,530 --> 00:28:17,250
You were quite good, you know,

406
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:19,140
at ruling.

407
00:28:19,830 --> 00:28:22,090
During your brief tenure as Hand.

408
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:24,250
I didn't rule, I was a servant.

409
00:28:24,250 --> 00:28:26,740
Still, a man of talent.

410
00:28:26,740 --> 00:28:28,240
Managed to kill a lot of people?

411
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:32,330
Yes, but you showed great promise in other areas as well.

412
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:37,770
She wanted me to leave King's Landing.

413
00:28:38,790 --> 00:28:40,120
She begged me.

414
00:28:40,640 --> 00:28:41,930
I wouldn't go.

415
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:43,280
Why?

416
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:44,760
'Cause I liked it.

417
00:28:46,030 --> 00:28:47,210
power...

418
00:28:47,870 --> 00:28:49,290
even as a servant.

419
00:28:49,890 --> 00:28:51,580
People follow leaders

420
00:28:52,980 --> 00:28:54,680
and they will never follow us.

421
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:56,530
They find us repulsive.

422
00:28:56,530 --> 00:28:58,010
I find us repulsive.

423
00:28:58,010 --> 00:29:00,000
And we find them repulsive,

424
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:03,390
which is why we surround ourselves with large comfortable boxes

425
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:04,770
to keep them away.

426
00:29:05,530 --> 00:29:06,620
And yet...

427
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:09,240
no matter what we do...

428
00:29:09,810 --> 00:29:14,220
people like you and me are never really satisfied inside the box.

429
00:29:14,290 --> 00:29:15,480
Not for long.

430
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:18,340
You're right.

431
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:21,320
- Let's go for a walk. - No.

432
00:29:21,350 --> 00:29:23,830
How many dwarves are there in the world?

433
00:29:24,650 --> 00:29:26,730
Is Cersei going to kill them all?

434
00:29:31,300 --> 00:29:32,650
Not him.

435
00:29:33,020 --> 00:29:35,080
Are you trying to deceive your queen?

436
00:29:35,390 --> 00:29:37,350
Shall I throw them in a cell, Your Grace?

437
00:29:37,630 --> 00:29:39,220
That won't be necessary, Ser Meryn.

438
00:29:39,220 --> 00:29:41,660
I don't want to dissuade the other hunters.

439
00:29:42,190 --> 00:29:43,680
Mistakes will be made.

440
00:29:43,680 --> 00:29:44,570
- Thank you, Your Grace. - Thanks.

441
00:29:44,580 --> 00:29:45,630
- Thank you, Your Grace. - Thank you.

442
00:29:45,630 --> 00:29:46,510
Take the head.

443
00:29:46,510 --> 00:29:47,330
Pardon me,  your Grace.

444
00:29:47,330 --> 00:29:49,500
I would take it if you don't mind.

445
00:29:49,510 --> 00:29:51,600
It could prove useful for my work.

446
00:29:52,850 --> 00:29:54,040
Very good.

447
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:58,560
Over there will be fine.

448
00:30:00,180 --> 00:30:02,290
You heard the man, over there.

449
00:30:30,380 --> 00:30:31,820
You're the hand of the King.

450
00:30:31,820 --> 00:30:33,120
No, uncle.

451
00:30:33,350 --> 00:30:36,840
Clearly it would not be appropriate for a woman to assume that role.

452
00:30:37,120 --> 00:30:38,540
I'm merely advising my son until

453
00:30:38,540 --> 00:30:41,250
he comes of age and chooses a Hand for himself.

454
00:30:41,560 --> 00:30:43,300
Your Grace, I would be willing

455
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:45,420
to serve provisionally as the King's Hand

456
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:46,830
until he becomes old enough.

457
00:30:46,830 --> 00:30:48,170
You're a good man, Lord Tyrell,

458
00:30:48,170 --> 00:30:49,990
but I don't imagine you'll have the time.

459
00:30:50,340 --> 00:30:52,590
In addition to be Master of Ships,

460
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:55,120
the King has appointed you Master of Coin.

461
00:30:56,850 --> 00:30:57,870
Oh, Your Grace.

462
00:30:57,870 --> 00:31:01,930
He called your experience and wisdom in financial matters unparalleled.

463
00:31:02,220 --> 00:31:03,910
He said he would be honored

464
00:31:03,910 --> 00:31:06,590
to have you represent the Crown's interest in the same.

465
00:31:06,590 --> 00:31:08,260
The honor is all mine, Your Grace.

466
00:31:08,650 --> 00:31:11,630
Y-Y-Your Grace, in the past, on several occasions,

467
00:31:11,630 --> 00:31:14,320
a Grand Maester has served as the King's Hand.

468
00:31:14,320 --> 00:31:18,950
The King has named Qyburn the new Master of Whispers.

469
00:31:20,870 --> 00:31:21,820
Your Grace,

470
00:31:21,820 --> 00:31:26,770
him? This-this man? Th-This embarrassment to the Citadel?

471
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:28,270
Your Grace,

472
00:31:28,810 --> 00:31:32,200
what qualifications can he possibly have for this post?

473
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:34,880
The qualification of loyalty, Grand Maester.

474
00:31:34,880 --> 00:31:37,150
That's far more than the eunuch ever had.

475
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:39,720
Far more than many ever have.

476
00:31:40,470 --> 00:31:42,260
I must say... I cannot see how...

477
00:31:42,260 --> 00:31:43,460
Uncle Kevan,

478
00:31:43,460 --> 00:31:46,730
in light of your position as Commander of the Lannister Armies,

479
00:31:46,790 --> 00:31:50,090
it would please the King if you would serve as his Master of War.

480
00:31:50,410 --> 00:31:53,130
No man living better deserves the title.

481
00:31:53,660 --> 00:31:55,320
That is kind of you to say.

482
00:31:55,850 --> 00:31:58,270
I would like to hear it from the King himself.

483
00:31:58,270 --> 00:31:59,750
Well, the King is very busy at this moment.

484
00:31:59,750 --> 00:32:02,300
He should be here learning what it means to rule.

485
00:32:02,300 --> 00:32:03,540
He is learning.

486
00:32:03,750 --> 00:32:06,020
On this occasion, in his capacity as ruler,

487
00:32:06,020 --> 00:32:08,010
he's asked me to speak on his behalf.

488
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:11,940
I returned to the capital to pay my respects to my brother,

489
00:32:12,310 --> 00:32:13,440
and to you,

490
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:14,890
and to serve the King.

491
00:32:15,250 --> 00:32:18,840
I did not return to the capital to serve as your puppet.

492
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:22,470
To watch you stack the Small Council with sycophants.

493
00:32:23,390 --> 00:32:25,020
Sending your own brother away so he won't be present.

494
00:32:25,020 --> 00:32:26,580
My brother has left the capital

495
00:32:26,580 --> 00:32:28,900
to lead a sensitive diplomatic mission.

496
00:32:28,900 --> 00:32:29,960
What mission?

497
00:32:29,960 --> 00:32:32,330
That is not your concern as Master of War.

498
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:37,020
I do not recognize your authority to dictate

499
00:32:37,020 --> 00:32:39,480
what is and is not my concern.

500
00:32:40,020 --> 00:32:41,430
You are the Queen Mother.

501
00:32:42,490 --> 00:32:43,820
Nothing more.

502
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:49,720
You would abandon your king and his time of need?

503
00:32:49,740 --> 00:32:52,570
If he wants to send for me, I will be waiting for him

504
00:32:53,110 --> 00:32:54,700
at Casterly Rock.

505
00:33:02,620 --> 00:33:04,780
Come on, you know this one.

506
00:33:06,670 --> 00:33:08,080
It looks like an animal.

507
00:33:11,220 --> 00:33:12,360
Snake.

508
00:33:12,940 --> 00:33:15,360
S-S-Sn... "S".

509
00:33:15,360 --> 00:33:17,940
- It's an "S". - Right, very good.

510
00:33:19,870 --> 00:33:22,340
Did you know that the youngest Lord Commander in history,

511
00:33:22,340 --> 00:33:24,870
Osric Stark, was elected at the age of 10?

512
00:33:26,830 --> 00:33:28,480
I know "S".

513
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:30,190
You'll learn, I promise.

514
00:33:30,450 --> 00:33:31,230
I taught Ser Davos,

515
00:33:31,230 --> 00:33:33,420
and old people are terrible at learning new things.

516
00:33:33,420 --> 00:33:35,580
Well, you are a wonderful teacher.

517
00:33:37,130 --> 00:33:38,350
Very patient.

518
00:33:38,350 --> 00:33:41,400
I only said that the more time that you spend practicing,

519
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:42,490
the faster you will be able to read.

520
00:33:42,500 --> 00:33:43,680
That's all right.

521
00:33:44,150 --> 00:33:45,510
We're doing just fine.

522
00:33:45,510 --> 00:33:49,840
I'm sure you and Ostrich Stark have a lot to talk about.

523
00:33:52,940 --> 00:33:55,260
How old were you when you learned how to read?

524
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:56,880
- Three. - Three?

525
00:33:56,960 --> 00:33:58,510
Who taught you, your mother?

526
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,200
No,

527
00:34:00,200 --> 00:34:01,760
old Maester Cressen did.

528
00:34:02,170 --> 00:34:03,600
I had a lot of time to practice.

529
00:34:03,600 --> 00:34:05,610
My mother kept me inside because...

530
00:34:08,410 --> 00:34:12,190
What do you call it in the south? What happened to your face.

531
00:34:12,430 --> 00:34:13,640
Grayscale.

532
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:16,230
What would you call it in the north of the Wall?

533
00:34:17,030 --> 00:34:18,300
I don't know.

534
00:34:19,230 --> 00:34:22,350
But two of my sisters had it. They both died.

535
00:34:22,780 --> 00:34:24,330
How did they cure you?

536
00:34:24,330 --> 00:34:26,910
I don't remember. I was a baby.

537
00:34:27,130 --> 00:34:29,370
A lot of people came and tried, I think.

538
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:31,370
Whatever they did, it went away.

539
00:34:33,490 --> 00:34:35,120
What happened to your sisters?

540
00:34:37,410 --> 00:34:41,490
My father made them move out of the keep into the huts outside.

541
00:34:42,240 --> 00:34:44,170
None of us were allowed to go near them.

542
00:34:44,460 --> 00:34:47,990
But we heard them, especially at night.

543
00:34:49,060 --> 00:34:53,310
They started to sound not like themselves.

544
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:55,440
Did you ever see them?

545
00:34:56,520 --> 00:34:58,110
Only once at the end.

546
00:35:00,130 --> 00:35:01,510
They were covered with it...

547
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:05,380
their faces, their arms.

548
00:35:06,430 --> 00:35:08,050
They acted like animals.

549
00:35:09,260 --> 00:35:12,280
My father had to drag them out to the woods on a rope.

550
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:15,030
What did he do with them in the woods?

551
00:35:20,710 --> 00:35:21,950
Mother.

552
00:35:22,290 --> 00:35:23,380
Leave us.

553
00:35:26,900 --> 00:35:28,090
Your Grace.

554
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:31,290
You need to stay away from that girl.

555
00:35:31,290 --> 00:35:32,830
- Why? - She's a wildling.

556
00:35:32,830 --> 00:35:34,130
Her name is Gilly.

557
00:35:34,220 --> 00:35:36,030
She's nice. I'm teaching her to read.

558
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:39,260
She's a wildling. Your father defeated her people.

559
00:35:39,260 --> 00:35:41,930
He executed their king for treason.

560
00:35:42,270 --> 00:35:45,160
They could strike at him by striking at you.

561
00:35:45,270 --> 00:35:46,720
Gilly wouldn't do that.

562
00:35:48,510 --> 00:35:50,690
You have no idea what people will do.

563
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:53,930
All your books and you still don't know.

564
00:36:00,100 --> 00:36:02,330
I ordered Mance Rayder burned at the stake.

565
00:36:02,730 --> 00:36:05,030
You prevented that order from being carried out.

566
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:07,360
You showed mercy to Mance Rayder.

567
00:36:07,820 --> 00:36:09,380
A King's word is law.

568
00:36:10,270 --> 00:36:11,270
Perhaps you should ask Ser Davos

569
00:36:11,270 --> 00:36:14,120
how much mercy I show to lawbreakers.

570
00:36:17,780 --> 00:36:19,950
Show too much kindness, people won't fear you.

571
00:36:19,950 --> 00:36:21,720
If they don't fear you, they don't follow you.

572
00:36:22,750 --> 00:36:25,150
With respect, Your Grace, the free folk will never follow you

573
00:36:25,150 --> 00:36:26,440
no matter what you do.

574
00:36:27,740 --> 00:36:29,770
You're the man who burned their king alive.

575
00:36:30,270 --> 00:36:31,450
Who, then?

576
00:36:33,540 --> 00:36:34,720
You?

577
00:36:34,990 --> 00:36:38,110
No. Only one of their own.

578
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,880
Do you know this wretched girl?

579
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:46,060
- Lyanna Mormont. - The Lord Commander's niece.

580
00:36:46,470 --> 00:36:48,000
Lady of Bear Island

581
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:49,860
and a child of ten.

582
00:36:51,390 --> 00:36:54,330
I asked her to commit her house to my cause. That's her response.

583
00:36:54,570 --> 00:36:57,710
"Bear Island knows no king but the King in the North,

584
00:36:57,730 --> 00:36:59,520
whose name is Stark."

585
00:37:00,050 --> 00:37:01,450
That amuses you.

586
00:37:03,690 --> 00:37:05,140
I apologize, Your Grace.

587
00:37:06,290 --> 00:37:09,940
Northerners can be a bit like the free folk.

588
00:37:10,850 --> 00:37:12,210
Loyal to their own.

589
00:37:12,930 --> 00:37:13,830
I know.

590
00:37:13,830 --> 00:37:15,450
My brother Robert went on often

591
00:37:15,450 --> 00:37:18,360
and loudly about how difficult it was to control them.

592
00:37:20,690 --> 00:37:22,480
Even with your father's help.

593
00:37:25,430 --> 00:37:28,660
Tonight, the Night's Watch elect a new Lord Commander.

594
00:37:29,530 --> 00:37:31,220
Ser Alliser Thorne is going to win.

595
00:37:31,220 --> 00:37:33,250
- Most likely. - One pleasant man.

596
00:37:33,800 --> 00:37:35,260
He thinks you're a traitor.

597
00:37:36,500 --> 00:37:38,040
What's your life gonna be like here at the Wall

598
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:39,460
with Thorne in command?

599
00:37:39,460 --> 00:37:40,820
Unpleasant, I expect.

600
00:37:40,830 --> 00:37:42,640
Your bravery made him look weak.

601
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:45,620
He'll punish you for it.

602
00:37:45,870 --> 00:37:47,840
I don't punish men for bravery.

603
00:37:47,840 --> 00:37:49,120
I reward them.

604
00:37:49,680 --> 00:37:51,380
I don't doubt it, Your Grace.

605
00:37:52,630 --> 00:37:54,520
But I'm a brother of the Night's Watch.

606
00:37:54,810 --> 00:37:57,310
I pledged them my life, my honor, my sword.

607
00:37:57,690 --> 00:37:59,700
I don't know what I have left to give you.

608
00:37:59,700 --> 00:38:01,510
You can give me the North.

609
00:38:02,890 --> 00:38:04,820
I can't.

610
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:08,060
Even if I wanted to, I'm a bastard.

611
00:38:08,300 --> 00:38:09,390
A Snow.

612
00:38:09,820 --> 00:38:12,530
Kneel before me. Lay your sword at my feet.

613
00:38:12,530 --> 00:38:15,460
Pledge me your service and you'll rise again as Jon Stark,

614
00:38:15,460 --> 00:38:16,940
Lord of Winterfell.

615
00:38:22,810 --> 00:38:25,340
He'll make you a Stark with the stroke of a pen.

616
00:38:25,560 --> 00:38:28,000
It's the first thing I ever remember wanting.

617
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:31,980
I daydreamed that my father would ask the king

618
00:38:32,030 --> 00:38:34,510
and just like that, I would never be the Bastard of Winterfell again.

619
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:37,490
No, you deserve that. You do.

620
00:38:37,490 --> 00:38:39,710
I-I couldn't be happier for you.

621
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:42,270
I'm gonna refuse him.

622
00:38:44,250 --> 00:38:45,230
But...

623
00:38:45,430 --> 00:38:47,520
you'd be Lord of Winterfell.

624
00:38:48,190 --> 00:38:50,560
I swore a vow to the Night's Watch.

625
00:38:50,560 --> 00:38:52,090
If I don't take my own word seriously,

626
00:38:52,090 --> 00:38:54,340
what sort of Lord of Winterfell would I be?

627
00:38:59,500 --> 00:39:03,120
Crowded, You'd think we were serving venison stew.

628
00:39:09,730 --> 00:39:14,130
Does anyone wish to speak for candidates...

629
00:39:14,580 --> 00:39:17,040
before we cast our tokens...

630
00:39:17,330 --> 00:39:21,800
for the 998th Lord Commander

631
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:23,630
of the Night's Watch?

632
00:39:25,870 --> 00:39:27,610
Ser Alliser Thorne is not just a knight,

633
00:39:27,620 --> 00:39:29,480
he's a man of true nobility.

634
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:32,440
He was Acting Commander when the Wall came under attack

635
00:39:32,440 --> 00:39:34,330
and led us to victory against the wildlings.

636
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:35,260
Hear. Hear.

637
00:39:35,260 --> 00:39:36,790
He's a veteran of 100 battles

638
00:39:36,790 --> 00:39:40,140
and has been a defender of the Watch and the Wall almost all of his life.

639
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:43,800
- He's the only true choice. - Hear.

640
00:39:43,800 --> 00:39:45,560
Hear.

641
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:50,790
Ser Denys Mallister joined the Watch as a boy

642
00:39:50,790 --> 00:39:54,410
and has served loyally longer than any of the Ranger.

643
00:39:54,700 --> 00:39:56,540
- That's right. - Through 10 winters he served.

644
00:39:56,540 --> 00:39:58,600
As Commander of the Shadow Tower...

645
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:00,570
he kept the wildlings away.

646
00:40:00,870 --> 00:40:02,390
We could do no better.

647
00:40:06,430 --> 00:40:08,460
If there's no one else...

648
00:40:08,460 --> 00:40:10,440
we will begin the voting.

649
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:15,370
The triangular tokens count for Ser Alliser Thorne.

650
00:40:15,660 --> 00:40:19,760
The square tokens for Ser Denys Mallister. Each brother...

651
00:40:20,140 --> 00:40:21,480
Maester Aemon...

652
00:40:23,900 --> 00:40:26,610
Samwell Tarly, go on.

653
00:40:27,780 --> 00:40:29,420
Sam the Slayer.

654
00:40:30,850 --> 00:40:33,940
Another wildling lover just like his friend Jon Snow.

655
00:40:34,040 --> 00:40:35,910
How's your lady love, Slayer?

656
00:40:36,680 --> 00:40:38,230
Her name is Gilly.

657
00:40:38,750 --> 00:40:40,630
Brother Slynt knows her quite well.

658
00:40:40,660 --> 00:40:41,620
They cowered together in

659
00:40:41,620 --> 00:40:43,800
the larder during the battle for the Wall.

660
00:40:44,460 --> 00:40:45,650
Lies!

661
00:40:45,710 --> 00:40:48,270
A wildling girl, a baby,

662
00:40:48,830 --> 00:40:50,500
and Lord Janos.

663
00:40:50,910 --> 00:40:52,860
I found him there after the battle was over.

664
00:40:52,860 --> 00:40:54,620
In a puddle of his own making.

665
00:40:58,660 --> 00:41:03,290
Whilst Lord Janos was hiding with the women and children

666
00:41:03,630 --> 00:41:05,390
Jon Snow was leading.

667
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:08,550
Ser Alliser fought bravely, it is true,

668
00:41:08,550 --> 00:41:10,750
but when he was wounded, it was Jon who saved us.

669
00:41:10,750 --> 00:41:13,550
He took charge of the Wall's defense,

670
00:41:13,560 --> 00:41:15,860
he killed the Magnar of the Thenns,

671
00:41:16,100 --> 00:41:18,370
he went North to deal with Mance Rayder.

672
00:41:18,370 --> 00:41:21,170
Knowing it almost certainly meant his own death.

673
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:26,070
Before that,

674
00:41:27,380 --> 00:41:30,550
he lead the mission to avenge the Lord Commander Mormont.

675
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:35,110
Mormont himself chose Jon to be his steward.

676
00:41:35,110 --> 00:41:36,750
He saw something in Jon

677
00:41:36,750 --> 00:41:38,890
and now we've all seen it, too.

678
00:41:39,460 --> 00:41:40,760
He may be young,

679
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:44,070
but he's the commander we turned to

680
00:41:44,070 --> 00:41:45,940
when the night was darkest.

681
00:41:45,940 --> 00:41:47,290
Hear.

682
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:54,540
Aye.

683
00:41:55,060 --> 00:41:56,990
Can't argue with any of that.

684
00:41:58,110 --> 00:42:00,640
But who does Jon Snow want to command?

685
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:02,430
The Night's Watch

686
00:42:03,990 --> 00:42:05,930
or the wildlings?

687
00:42:06,150 --> 00:42:09,410
Everyone knows he loved a wildling girl.

688
00:42:09,410 --> 00:42:11,440
Spoke with Mance Rayder many times.

689
00:42:11,440 --> 00:42:12,090
What would have happened

690
00:42:12,100 --> 00:42:15,190
in that tent between those two old friends

691
00:42:15,190 --> 00:42:17,580
if Stannis's army hadn't come along?

692
00:42:17,650 --> 00:42:22,470
We all saw him put the King-Beyond-the-Wall out of his misery.

693
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:26,310
Do you want to choose a man who has fought the wildlings all his life

694
00:42:26,610 --> 00:42:28,440
or a man who makes love to them?

695
00:42:36,510 --> 00:42:37,890
It is time!

696
00:43:24,770 --> 00:43:26,880
It appears to be a tie, maester.

697
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:48,990
Jon Snow! Jon Snow!

698
00:43:48,990 --> 00:43:50,550
Snow! Snow!

699
00:43:50,550 --> 00:43:52,440
Snow! Snow!

700
00:44:22,060 --> 00:44:24,630
You! You!

701
00:44:28,200 --> 00:44:29,410
What have you got there?

702
00:44:32,400 --> 00:44:35,240
- I said... - Turn around and go!

703
00:44:37,660 --> 00:44:38,880
Turn around...

704
00:44:39,550 --> 00:44:41,910
- and go! - That's a nice little sword.

705
00:44:42,160 --> 00:44:44,410
Worth a hundred pieces, a sword like that.

706
00:44:46,730 --> 00:44:48,820
Nothing's worth anything to dead men.

707
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:54,450
Quickly, go! Go!

708
00:45:07,900 --> 00:45:09,170
Who are you?

709
00:45:10,010 --> 00:45:11,750
Why were they scared of you?

710
00:45:12,110 --> 00:45:13,510
You lost this.

711
00:45:24,830 --> 00:45:27,120
You said there was no Jaqen H'ghar here.

712
00:45:27,350 --> 00:45:28,490
There isn't.

713
00:45:28,810 --> 00:45:30,960
A man is not Jaqen H'ghar.

714
00:45:33,430 --> 00:45:34,760
Who are you, then?

715
00:45:36,340 --> 00:45:37,400
No one.

716
00:45:37,890 --> 00:45:40,010
And that is who a girl must become.

717
00:46:52,030 --> 00:46:53,960
Why?

718
00:48:53,930 --> 00:48:54,890
Mhysa!

719
00:48:54,890 --> 00:48:55,980
Mhysa!

720
00:48:56,260 --> 00:48:57,390
Mhysa!

721
00:48:57,620 --> 00:49:00,180
Mhysa! Mhysa!

722
00:49:03,370 --> 00:49:04,530
She should have cut the traitor's

723
00:49:04,530 --> 00:49:06,880
head in the Great Pyramid and be done with it.

724
00:49:06,880 --> 00:49:09,040
Which is what I keep telling her to do to you.

725
00:49:13,290 --> 00:49:14,500
Mhysa!

726
00:50:33,970 --> 00:50:35,210
Mhysa!

727
00:51:11,050 --> 00:51:12,730
Mhysa!

728
00:52:16,130 --> 00:52:18,650
I'll stand guard outside your door tonight, Your Grace.

729
00:52:18,660 --> 00:52:20,420
We all guard tonight.

730
00:52:21,850 --> 00:52:22,950
Leave me.

731
00:53:16,020 --> 00:53:17,240
Drogon.

